# SABOTAGE: T163 / ADR-051 R6 — the quota check FAILS OPEN: its single error arm answers
# `{:ok, true}`, so an org with no limit row, an ambiguous limit, or a subscription whose
# period the mirror has not rolled over is told it is within its quota. An absent limit
# silently becomes an unlimited one.
#
# Flips the no-limit-row test. Its positive control (a real row answers) and every
# within/over test stay green (a readable limit still answers correctly), which is
# exactly why this regression would pass a suite that only tests the happy path.
# APP: demo
# TEST_FILES: test/usage_quota_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: no entitlement row carrying the metric is an error, never {:ok, true}
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/quota.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/quota.ex
index 325ae84..8442a26 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/quota.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/quota.ex
@@ -73,7 +73,8 @@ defmodule Samen.Billing.Quota do
       {:ok, within?}
     else
       # Every unreadable limit or period lands here, and stays an error (R6).
-      {:error, reason} -> {:error, reason}
+      # SABOTAGE (ADR-051 R6): an unreadable limit is treated as within it.
+      {:error, _reason} -> {:ok, true}
     end
   rescue
     e -> {:error, e}
